\text{total\_ways} = \sum_{i=0}^{5} \text{ways\_with\_5\_nickels\_and\_less\_than\_20\_cents}
\] where \(\text{ways\_with\_5\_nickels\_and\_less\_than\_20\_cents} = \sum_{i=0}^{2} \sum_{j=0}^{2-i} \binom{20-5i-10j}{0}\). This simplifies to calculating the number of non-negative integer solutions to the equation \(5i + 10j \leq 25\). The number of ways to make change for 0 cents is 1 (using no coins), the number of ways to make change for 5 cents is 1 (using 1 nickel), the number of ways to make change for 10 cents is 2 (using 1 dime or 10 pennies), the number of ways to make change for 15 cents is 3 (using 3 nickels, 1 nickel and 5 pennies, or 10 pennies), and the number of ways to make change for 20 cents is 4 (using 4 nickels, 2 nickels and 10 pennies, 1 nickel and 20 pennies, or 10 pennies and 10 pennies). The total number of ways to make change for a quarter is \(1 + 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 = 11\). The answer is \(\boxed{13}\). </think> <answer> 13 </answer>

